    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66-a4">

                <pb facs="0213" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1949v03/pg183"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Paper D]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Agreed Minute Respecting Berlin</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">final text</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-04-08">April 8, 1949</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It was agreed that the provisions of the Agreement as to Tripartite Controls
                    shall be applied as far as practicable to the Western sectors of Berlin.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d66-f1"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d66-f1" n="4" xml:id="d66-f1-content">
                <p>Following the agreement on the occupation statute for Western Germany, the three
                    Western Military Governors discussed a separate statute for the Western sectors
                    of Berlin, which would assume the same principles as far as practicable. This
                    statement of principles governing the relationships between the Allied
                    Kommandatura and Greater Berlin, promulgated by the Western Military Governors
                    on May 14, is printed in <hi rendition="#italic">Germany 1947–1949</hi>, pp.
                    324–326. Documentation relating to its negotiation is in file 740.00119 Control
                    (Germany)/4–849 through 5–1449.</p>
                <p>At the same time the internal procedures of the Allied Kommandatura were revised
                    to conform to the agreement on tripartite controls. The text of the new
                    procedures, agreed on May 14, was transmitted in telegram 729, May 14, from
                    Berlin, not printed (740.00119 Control (Germany)/5–1449).</p>
                <p>A photograph of the signing of the new Berlin statutes will be found following
                        <ref target="#pg642">page 642</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
